Modifications made in this repository
-------------------------------------

1. Go module path
   `github.com/nezhahq/nezha` -> `github.com/CyL-Cly/wushang-panel`
   All internal import paths and `.goreleaser.yml` ldflags were rewritten
   accordingly. Third-party dependencies under the `github.com/nezhahq/`
   prefix (libdns-tencentcloud) are external modules and were left unchanged.

2. Admin frontend vendored
   The dashboard frontend now lives in `admin-frontend/` inside this
   repository. `script/build-frontends.sh` builds `admin-frontend/` and
   installs the output into `cmd/dashboard/admin-dist`, which is embedded
   into the dashboard binary. The user frontend is no longer required to be
   a local checkout; when absent, `script/fetch-frontends.sh` supplies the
   prebuilt upstream release.

3. Frontend bundle policy
   `admin-frontend/vite.config.ts` keeps route-level lazy loading and removes
   the catch-all `vendor` chunk. The additional hand-written
   `motion`/`table`/`terminal`/`icons`/`ui-kit` groups added in the upstream
   pull request were dropped; chunking is left to Rollup's dependency
   analysis.

4. Retained upstream performance changes
   The following changes from nezhahq/nezha PR #1245 are kept in this build:
   static asset compression and caching, static ETag with content digests,
   SPA fallback 404 preservation, and the viewer-scoped server-list
   singleflight with per-request slice cloning.

5. Second-party identification
   `service/singleton.BuildFlavor = "wushang-panel"` is exposed through the
   settings API as `flavor`, and the admin UI footer labels the build
   accordingly. The frontend template entry for `admin-dist` now points at
   this repository and leaves `version` empty so `fetch-frontends.sh` does not
   overwrite the embedded build with an upstream release.

6. CI and repository automation
   Upstream release, AtomGit/Gitee sync, contributors and CodeQL workflows
   were removed, as were the vuepress-era helper scripts. Only
   `.github/workflows/test.yml` remains, with the cross-repository agent
   checkout repointed to `CyL-Cly/wushang-agent`.

7. Documentation
   README, issue templates and NOTICE updated to identify this as a
   second-party build.

Compliance notes
----------------

The `admin-dist` and `user-dist` directories are build artifacts and are
excluded from version control (only `.gitkeep` files are tracked). They are
produced at build time from the sources in this repository.

This is an unofficial build. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the
Nezha Monitoring project, and changes made here are not contributed back
upstream.
